1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:53,058
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00:53,328 --> 00:00:54,444
[Six Years Ago] Let's have one more drink.

3
00:00:54,444 --> 00:00:56,068
You've had too much.

4
00:00:56,068 --> 00:00:57,528
Just one more drink, I swear.

5
00:00:57,528 --> 00:00:59,283
No, no. You need to go home.

6
00:00:59,283 --> 00:01:01,149
Excuse me, sir. Have a drink with me.

7
00:01:01,149 --> 00:01:03,656
- These punks won't drink with me. - He's lost his mind.

8
00:01:03,656 --> 00:01:05,580
- I'm sorry. - No, don't apologize.

9
00:01:05,580 --> 00:01:06,672
It's okay. Let me go.

10
00:01:06,672 --> 00:01:08,616
- Wait... - I'm fine, let go.

11
00:01:08,616 --> 00:01:10,340
Is the taxi here yet?

12
00:01:10,340 --> 00:01:11,849
- Well, it's... - Come on, let's drink.

13
00:01:11,849 --> 00:01:13,016
What's wrong with you?

14
00:01:13,016 --> 00:01:15,176
- Seriously... - Jeez.

15
00:01:15,176 --> 00:01:16,328
It's on its way.

16
00:01:16,328 --> 00:01:17,357
- It's not here. - Over here!

17
00:01:17,357 --> 00:01:18,904
- It's here, it's here. - It's here?

18
00:01:18,904 --> 00:01:21,028
Oh, man.

19
00:01:21,028 --> 00:01:22,508
- Where are we going? - Mapo.

20
00:01:22,508 --> 00:01:24,078
- To Mapo, right? - That's where you live, sir.

21
00:01:24,078 --> 00:01:25,265
- Is that where I live? - Yeah.

22
00:01:25,265 --> 00:01:27,076
Alright, I'm fine.

23
00:01:27,076 --> 00:01:30,296
- Okay. - Let go. Wait. Just stay still.

24
00:01:30,296 --> 00:01:32,016
- Darn it. - What is it?

25
00:01:32,016 --> 00:01:34,084
- Twenty thousand won for Sun Hyuk. - Thank you.

26
00:01:34,084 --> 00:01:35,672
- Twenty thousand won for Eun Tae too. - Oh.

27
00:01:35,672 --> 00:01:36,936
- Take a taxi home. - Thank you.

28
00:01:36,936 --> 00:01:38,816
- Get home safe, sir. - Hey, I don't have any money.

29
00:01:38,816 --> 00:01:40,083
- Give me ten thousand won. - Just ten thousand won.

30
00:01:40,083 --> 00:01:41,416
- I don't have any. - Me?

31
00:01:41,416 --> 00:01:42,949
I don't have any, yeah.

32
00:01:42,949 --> 00:01:43,949
- Goodbye, sir. - Wait, no.

33
00:01:43,949 --> 00:01:45,083
With this money, let's get a...

34
00:01:45,083 --> 00:01:46,316
No way!

35
00:01:46,316 --> 00:01:47,483
Ouch, it hurts so much.

36
00:01:47,483 --> 00:01:48,549
It hurts!

37
00:01:48,549 --> 00:01:50,716
By the way, my bag.

38
00:01:50,716 --> 00:01:53,783
- Oh, here you go. - This isn't mine. Mine!

39
00:01:53,783 --> 00:01:55,952
Can't you get a grip?

40
00:01:55,952 --> 00:01:59,283
You two aren't going out for drinks without me, are you?

41
00:01:59,283 --> 00:02:00,283
Of course not, sir.

42
00:02:00,283 --> 00:02:01,836
- Really? - Go ahead. Get home safe.

43
00:02:01,836 --> 00:02:05,204
- Really? You two, go home. - Get home safe, sir.

44
00:02:05,204 --> 00:02:07,283
Darn, that was exhausting.

45
00:02:10,816 --> 00:02:13,449
It took us 30 minutes to get him home.

46
00:02:13,449 --> 00:02:15,488
That's faster than he used to be.

47
00:02:15,488 --> 00:02:17,624
He used to sleep on the street.

48
00:02:17,624 --> 00:02:19,883
Will you end up like that when you become a team leader?

49
00:02:19,883 --> 00:02:21,016
Why?

50
00:02:21,016 --> 00:02:24,128
If I become a team leader, will you take me home?

51
00:02:24,128 --> 00:02:25,652
I'm taking you home tonight too.

52
00:02:25,652 --> 00:02:29,616
Oh, Gong!

53
00:02:30,649 --> 00:02:33,016
- Hey, come with me. - What?

54
00:02:33,016 --> 00:02:34,016
- Follow me. - Huh?

55
00:02:34,016 --> 00:02:36,749
- Come with me. - Where are we going?

56
00:02:36,749 --> 00:02:38,484
Do you buy lottery tickets?

57
00:02:38,484 --> 00:02:40,572
[Lottery Ticket Shop] I've bought a ticket once or twice.

58
00:02:40,572 --> 00:02:42,716
Alright, what day is it today?

59
00:02:43,496 --> 00:02:47,556
April 27th, 11:00...

60
00:02:47,556 --> 00:02:49,036
It's 11:42 PM.

61
00:02:49,036 --> 00:02:50,704
11:42 PM.

62
00:02:50,704 --> 00:02:52,224
What's the last digit of your employee number?

63
00:02:52,224 --> 00:02:53,376
My employee number?

64
00:02:53,376 --> 00:02:55,444
Oh, it's eight.

65
00:02:55,444 --> 00:02:58,324
Eight... then three.

66
00:02:58,324 --> 00:03:01,083
The rest, quick pick.

67
00:03:02,156 --> 00:03:03,856
Okay.

68
00:03:04,838 --> 00:03:07,044
- Sir, two of these, please. - Sure.

69
00:03:07,044 --> 00:03:09,083
- Okay. - Thanks.

70
00:03:10,560 --> 00:03:12,588
Here. One for me, one for you.

71
00:03:12,588 --> 00:03:14,349
Thank you.

72
00:03:15,449 --> 00:03:16,936
Do you buy it often?

73
00:03:16,936 --> 00:03:19,236
Whenever I see a shop, I'll buy one.

74
00:03:19,236 --> 00:03:20,808
You don't?

75
00:03:20,808 --> 00:03:23,784
I feel like I'd just get my hopes up for something I won't win anyway.

76
00:03:23,784 --> 00:03:26,983
Jeez. Who cares if you don't win?

77
00:03:26,983 --> 00:03:29,616
You buy them knowing you probably won't win?

78
00:03:29,616 --> 00:03:34,320
Doesn't it make this moment a little more meaningful?

79
00:03:34,320 --> 00:03:38,016
Work is always the same, and life isn't exactly exciting.

80
00:03:38,016 --> 00:03:40,949
But if you give it some meaning and buy a lottery ticket,

81
00:03:40,949 --> 00:03:44,349
today feels worth remembering.

82
00:03:44,349 --> 00:03:46,384
That's why I buy lottery tickets.

83
00:03:46,384 --> 00:03:49,016
Wow. That's kind of romantic.

84
00:03:49,016 --> 00:03:51,149
[Mannam Singing Room] Don't fall for me.

85
00:03:52,616 --> 00:03:54,420
But you never know.

86
00:03:54,420 --> 00:03:56,249
Out of eight billion people in the world,

87
00:03:56,249 --> 00:04:00,316
what are the odds you and I would meet?

88
00:04:00,316 --> 00:04:05,283
I don't know. One in a hundred million? No, wait. One in ten million?

89
00:04:05,283 --> 00:04:09,592
I don't know. But they say the lottery is one in eight million.

90
00:04:09,592 --> 00:04:12,520
Then the odds of us meeting are about the same

91
00:04:12,520 --> 00:04:15,488
as winning the lottery, aren't they?

92
00:04:15,488 --> 00:04:20,216
We met like this, so why couldn't we win the lottery too?

93
00:04:21,383 --> 00:04:22,564
I think we're gonna win.

94
00:04:22,564 --> 00:04:23,716
Oh.

95
00:04:23,716 --> 00:04:25,868
If this wins, we split it, okay?

96
00:04:25,868 --> 00:04:27,268
Jeez.

97
00:04:27,268 --> 00:04:28,968
Let's go.

98
00:04:30,116 --> 00:04:32,148
Oh, hey, my bag.

99
00:04:32,148 --> 00:04:34,016
Okay, thank you!

100
00:04:37,883 --> 00:04:44,783
[Episode 5, When No One Can Speak Their True Feelings]

101
00:04:57,656 --> 00:04:59,596
Well, look at this.

102
00:04:59,596 --> 00:05:02,848
Did everyone gather here because of me?

103
00:05:02,848 --> 00:05:04,649
Do you even realize what you did?

104
00:05:05,876 --> 00:05:07,920
So,

105
00:05:07,920 --> 00:05:11,796
now that you've caused a mess, are you scared and here to apologize?

106
00:05:11,796 --> 00:05:13,816
Or are you here to clean up your mess?

107
00:05:13,816 --> 00:05:16,256
Would apologizing make things okay?

108
00:05:16,256 --> 00:05:18,049
Of course, it wouldn't, you punk.

109
00:05:18,049 --> 00:05:21,972
Then what should I do?

110
00:05:21,972 --> 00:05:23,268
I'm not sure.

111
00:05:23,268 --> 00:05:26,883
Then what do you want me to do, Mr. Jang?

112
00:05:27,556 --> 00:05:28,904
What are you doing right now?

113
00:05:28,904 --> 00:05:30,656
Should I stay here,

114
00:05:30,656 --> 00:05:34,788
waste everyone's time, and just wait to get fired?

115
00:05:34,788 --> 00:05:37,983
Is that how you see yourself?

116
00:05:37,983 --> 00:05:42,044
Darn, I picked the wrong team leader.

117
00:05:42,044 --> 00:05:44,616
If I'd known you were like this, I never would've made you team leader.

118
00:05:44,616 --> 00:05:46,660
I'm sorry, but...

119
00:05:46,660 --> 00:05:49,820
I'm not here to apologize today. And I'm not here to clean up my mess either.

120
00:05:49,820 --> 00:05:51,916
Yeah, alright.

121
00:05:51,916 --> 00:05:55,549
Then go ahead and explain yourself.

122
00:05:55,549 --> 00:05:57,249
Explain myself?

123
00:05:58,304 --> 00:06:00,004
Well...

124
00:06:01,292 --> 00:06:03,883
What did I even do wrong?

125
00:06:04,912 --> 00:06:07,816
I can understand you siphoning off one of our clients.

126
00:06:07,816 --> 00:06:09,036
Actually,

127
00:06:09,036 --> 00:06:12,024
I don't like that either, but since Ms. Park approved it,

128
00:06:12,024 --> 00:06:13,356
I can let it slide.

129
00:06:13,356 --> 00:06:16,783
You were there when we first landed Mantua,

130
00:06:16,783 --> 00:06:18,648
so it's not like you had no part in it.

131
00:06:18,648 --> 00:06:20,149
However,

132
00:06:21,216 --> 00:06:24,183
if you're gonna leave, just slip out quietly on your own.

133
00:06:25,128 --> 00:06:27,716
Why are you trying to steal our employees?

134
00:06:27,716 --> 00:06:31,796
If Hongsung were the better company, they'd stay here.

135
00:06:31,796 --> 00:06:34,049
If not, they'll come to my company.

136
00:06:34,049 --> 00:06:36,800
How could I force them to leave?

137
00:06:36,800 --> 00:06:39,356
It's their decision.

138
00:06:39,356 --> 00:06:41,724
You make it sound so reasonable, huh?

139
00:06:41,724 --> 00:06:45,216
Fine. I'll give you a reasonable answer too.

140
00:06:45,216 --> 00:06:49,083
Do you really think the company will just let you walk away like this?

141
00:06:53,596 --> 00:06:55,268
Mr. Jang,

142
00:06:55,268 --> 00:06:59,704
do you think I'm doing this to get revenge on Hongsung?

143
00:06:59,704 --> 00:07:01,708
Me?

144
00:07:01,708 --> 00:07:03,283
I've been

145
00:07:03,283 --> 00:07:08,183
loyal to Hongsung for over ten years.

146
00:07:08,183 --> 00:07:11,083
If I could stay at Hongsung and keep doing my job,

147
00:07:11,083 --> 00:07:13,049
I'd stay here.

148
00:07:13,049 --> 00:07:15,549
If any employee chooses to follow me,

149
00:07:15,549 --> 00:07:17,516
it'll be the same for them.

150
00:07:17,516 --> 00:07:19,683
The truth is, Hongsung

151
00:07:20,476 --> 00:07:23,349
doesn't treat its people well, does it?

152
00:07:23,349 --> 00:07:27,483
I'm trying to give them what Hongsung can't.

153
00:07:28,932 --> 00:07:30,052
Mr. Jung.

154
00:07:30,052 --> 00:07:32,276
Yes.

155
00:07:32,276 --> 00:07:35,416
You think you're any different? Huh?

156
00:07:35,416 --> 00:07:37,483
You can't even run a team properly here,

157
00:07:37,483 --> 00:07:41,136
and you think you'll run a company and treat people well out there?

158
00:07:41,136 --> 00:07:44,360
Jeez, you're really talking nonsense.

159
00:07:44,360 --> 00:07:45,883
That's for me to prove.

160
00:07:45,883 --> 00:07:47,816
- Sun Hyuk! - Yes.

161
00:07:47,816 --> 00:07:51,552
This industry isn't as big as you think. It's a small pond.

162
00:07:51,552 --> 00:07:55,900
You think you can leave here, turn against us, and still do business?

163
00:07:55,900 --> 00:07:58,444
Are you actually worried about me?

164
00:07:58,444 --> 00:08:00,144
Yeah.

165
00:08:01,083 --> 00:08:04,483
I really am worried about you, man.

166
00:08:05,892 --> 00:08:09,336
I really appreciate your concern.

167
00:08:09,336 --> 00:08:10,816
But today,

168
00:08:10,816 --> 00:08:14,448
I'm here to ask you not to reprimand employees who had nothing to do with it.

169
00:08:14,448 --> 00:08:19,049
The employees I approached about leaving did nothing wrong.

170
00:08:19,049 --> 00:08:20,983
Could you do that for me?

171
00:08:24,520 --> 00:08:26,220
Jeez.

172
00:08:27,764 --> 00:08:30,983
I'll take it as a yes and get going. Take care.

173
00:08:31,680 --> 00:08:33,380
Take care.

174
00:08:41,436 --> 00:08:43,252
Mr. Gong.

175
00:08:43,252 --> 00:08:44,424
Yeah.

176
00:08:44,424 --> 00:08:46,549
Lock down Mantua quickly.

177
00:08:55,200 --> 00:08:57,916
That's why Mr. Jang stopped by.

178
00:08:57,916 --> 00:09:00,788
He asked to see Team 4's employment contracts.

179
00:09:00,788 --> 00:09:03,112
He was checking the non-compete clause.

180
00:09:03,112 --> 00:09:04,849
Is that clause enforceable?

181
00:09:04,849 --> 00:09:09,284
It's technically enforceable, but not really effective.

182
00:09:09,284 --> 00:09:11,316
It's iffy whether we could sue over it,

183
00:09:11,316 --> 00:09:13,816
and even if we did, there's no guarantee we'd win.

184
00:09:13,816 --> 00:09:16,500
And time would keep passing while the lawsuit dragged on,

185
00:09:16,500 --> 00:09:19,049
which works in Team Leader Jung's favor.

186
00:09:23,008 --> 00:09:25,764
Did you know Ms. Park came by a week ago too?

187
00:09:25,764 --> 00:09:27,283
- Really? - Yeah.

188
00:09:27,283 --> 00:09:29,649
She asked the exact same thing as Mr. Jang.

189
00:09:29,649 --> 00:09:32,504
So she wasn't planning to let it slide either.

190
00:09:32,504 --> 00:09:35,483
Of course, not. It's clearly misconduct.

191
00:09:35,483 --> 00:09:38,564
The higher-ups are sharper than you think.

192
00:09:38,564 --> 00:09:40,228
But do you know why

193
00:09:40,228 --> 00:09:42,844
Ms. Park didn't involve Legal Team?

194
00:09:42,844 --> 00:09:43,849
Why?

195
00:09:43,849 --> 00:09:47,849
If Legal Team gets involved, Internal Audit would naturally follow.

196
00:09:47,849 --> 00:09:51,149
Would you want to make a scandal even bigger?

197
00:09:51,149 --> 00:09:52,872
I don't know for sure,

198
00:09:52,872 --> 00:09:56,216
but maybe Mr. Jung factored that in too.

199
00:09:57,956 --> 00:10:00,849
But honestly, I don't know.

200
00:10:00,849 --> 00:10:04,449
I don't know whether to call Mr. Jung clever

201
00:10:04,449 --> 00:10:06,983
or feel sorry for him.

202
00:10:08,116 --> 00:10:10,183
I don't know either.

203
00:10:10,183 --> 00:10:13,416
Part of me just wants to root for him either way,

204
00:10:13,416 --> 00:10:17,749
but he keeps kicking away my light stick and telling me to take up the sword.

205
00:10:21,220 --> 00:10:23,028
A shoe boutique?

206
00:10:23,028 --> 00:10:25,456
Yes. We need to push this through urgently.

207
00:10:25,456 --> 00:10:26,960
Us?

208
00:10:26,960 --> 00:10:28,683
Wait, how did this happen?

209
00:10:30,200 --> 00:10:31,832
I caused a mess.

210
00:10:31,832 --> 00:10:33,083
Come on, Mr. Gong.

211
00:10:33,083 --> 00:10:36,592
At least give us a heads-up before you cause a mess.

212
00:10:36,592 --> 00:10:39,005
But can we really handle the Laknes launch

213
00:10:39,005 --> 00:10:41,360
and a shoe boutique with this team?

214
00:10:41,360 --> 00:10:45,560
Once we get the brand selection from Mantua, Ms. Park will approve the budget.

215
00:10:45,560 --> 00:10:48,484
Mr. Jang will handle any issues with the brands' headquarters.

216
00:10:48,484 --> 00:10:51,483
So we shouldn't have that much actual work to do.

217
00:10:52,152 --> 00:10:53,944
Well, Mr. Gong.

218
00:10:53,944 --> 00:10:57,883
Are we doing this because of Mr. Jung?

219
00:10:59,848 --> 00:11:01,704
No.

220
00:11:01,704 --> 00:11:04,049
We're doing it because the company needs it.

221
00:11:07,612 --> 00:11:09,592
Then the most important thing.

222
00:11:09,592 --> 00:11:10,996
What's the budget?

223
00:11:10,996 --> 00:11:12,052
[Mantova Shoes Boutique Contract]

224
00:11:12,052 --> 00:11:14,349
Three million euros.

225
00:11:15,528 --> 00:11:19,824
That's just the first order. It could go up to ten million euros later.

226
00:11:19,824 --> 00:11:21,096
What do you think?

227
00:11:21,096 --> 00:11:24,249
Is that enough to tempt Mantua?

228
00:11:24,249 --> 00:11:25,872
The numbers are more than enough.

229
00:11:25,872 --> 00:11:28,924
The numbers are enough. So what's worrying you?

230
00:11:28,924 --> 00:11:31,548
The people at Mantua aren't exactly reasonable.

231
00:11:31,548 --> 00:11:36,228
I'm more worried about how close you are to Mr. Jung.

232
00:11:36,228 --> 00:11:38,580
What do you think?

233
00:11:38,580 --> 00:11:41,384
Mr. Jang, did you forget that I proposed this?

234
00:11:41,384 --> 00:11:43,264
I know.

235
00:11:43,264 --> 00:11:47,049
And I know you didn't want to do this either.

236
00:11:50,136 --> 00:11:51,649
I don't care about the rest,

237
00:11:51,649 --> 00:11:56,283
but if you can't close the deal with that money, we've got a problem.

238
00:11:57,060 --> 00:11:59,296
I'll close the deal.

239
00:12:02,320 --> 00:12:04,020
Eun Tae.

240
00:12:05,048 --> 00:12:06,916
This is company business.

241
00:12:09,096 --> 00:12:10,692
Don't forget that.

242
00:12:10,692 --> 00:12:12,516
Yes, understood, sir.

243
00:12:13,583 --> 00:12:18,016
[22 Hours Before the Laknes Launch]

244
00:12:18,016 --> 00:12:20,708
Yes, Director, I saw the revisions. They look good.

245
00:12:20,708 --> 00:12:23,483
I've seen all the feeds you posted. They're all great, but...

246
00:12:23,483 --> 00:12:25,816
- Yes, that would be great. - Park No Eul, Lee Yeon Jung, Park Min Ah...

247
00:12:25,816 --> 00:12:28,883
- They didn't post any solo product shots. - Thank you, yes.

248
00:12:28,883 --> 00:12:30,028
Oh, yes, Team Leader.

249
00:12:30,028 --> 00:12:31,880
- It's not 30, right? - You received what I sent, right?

250
00:12:31,880 --> 00:12:33,649
- Did you open them to check the count? - Oh, yes, about that...

251
00:12:33,649 --> 00:12:35,883
- That's not the event from the proposal. - Oh.

252
00:12:35,883 --> 00:12:36,883
- If it's okay with you, - No, that's fine.

253
00:12:36,883 --> 00:12:39,316
- could you open just two and check? - I'm sorry for all the revisions.

254
00:12:39,316 --> 00:12:41,349
I'll buy you a nice meal after the launch.

255
00:12:41,349 --> 00:12:42,849
- Yes, please verify that. - Okay.

256
00:12:42,849 --> 00:12:46,516
- Oh, yes. Thank you so much. - Thank you.

257
00:13:00,624 --> 00:13:02,104
- What are you doing? - What did you say, you punk?

258
00:13:02,104 --> 00:13:03,683
- Huh? - What?

259
00:13:03,683 --> 00:13:05,444
I asked what you're doing.

260
00:13:06,912 --> 00:13:09,449
We're taking a break.

261
00:13:10,716 --> 00:13:12,449
Done resting?

262
00:13:13,992 --> 00:13:15,692
Let's go.

263
00:13:22,649 --> 00:13:25,549
[12 Hours Before the Laknes Launch]

264
00:13:34,983 --> 00:13:37,108
[9 Hours Before the Laknes Launch]

265
00:13:44,536 --> 00:13:45,983
- Ji Hye. - Yes?

266
00:13:45,983 --> 00:13:48,583
Pace yourself. This is a marathon.

267
00:13:48,583 --> 00:13:49,583
Okay.

268
00:13:49,583 --> 00:13:51,872
Gi Tae. Aren't you being a little too relaxed?

269
00:13:51,872 --> 00:13:53,208
At least try to keep up with Ji Hye.

270
00:13:53,208 --> 00:13:55,664
Well, it is a marathon.

271
00:13:56,664 --> 00:13:58,416
Looks like your hands are the slowest, Mr. Yang.

272
00:13:58,416 --> 00:14:00,624
Oh, Mr. Gong.

273
00:14:00,624 --> 00:14:02,883
Please take a seat.

274
00:14:05,052 --> 00:14:06,540
Sorry I'm late.

275
00:14:06,540 --> 00:14:09,284
Not at all, we're just getting started.

276
00:14:09,284 --> 00:14:10,664
What should I start with?

277
00:14:10,664 --> 00:14:12,532
Oh, you can put these stickers on.

278
00:14:12,532 --> 00:14:14,680
Peel this off and...

279
00:14:14,680 --> 00:14:17,183
But why did you come? We could've handled this ourselves.

280
00:14:17,183 --> 00:14:18,904
Laknes launches tomorrow, right?

281
00:14:18,904 --> 00:14:20,848
We also need to have one final check-in.

282
00:14:20,848 --> 00:14:22,548
Mr. Gong.

283
00:14:23,924 --> 00:14:26,496
The main banners in Gangnam and Sogong-dong are done.

284
00:14:26,496 --> 00:14:28,556
The influencer marketing campaign is done,

285
00:14:28,556 --> 00:14:31,348
the launch event is all checked, the inventory is checked,

286
00:14:31,348 --> 00:14:33,236
and we just need to finish the barcodes.

287
00:14:36,308 --> 00:14:39,912
The rest is in the hands of fate.

288
00:14:39,912 --> 00:14:43,264
Fate isn't gonna help us with the barcodes.

289
00:14:43,264 --> 00:14:46,816
Getting these done before tomorrow's launch is what matters.

290
00:14:46,816 --> 00:14:49,972
They say heaven helps those who help themselves.

291
00:14:49,972 --> 00:14:52,720
Jeez, he's getting cheeky.

292
00:14:52,720 --> 00:14:54,583
Hey, come here. Come here. I can't take this anymore!

293
00:14:54,583 --> 00:14:56,749
I'm doing all of these myself. All of them.

294
00:14:56,749 --> 00:14:58,316
- Come on, give it to me. - Don't touch.

295
00:14:58,316 --> 00:15:00,692
- Fine. I'll do it all. - I'm doing them.

296
00:15:00,692 --> 00:15:02,900
Just a moment.

297
00:15:02,900 --> 00:15:04,560
- Where are you going? - Just leave mine.

298
00:15:04,560 --> 00:15:06,744
I'll do it later.

299
00:15:06,744 --> 00:15:08,824
Doesn't Mr. Gong

300
00:15:08,824 --> 00:15:11,749
seem pretty excited these days?

301
00:15:12,756 --> 00:15:15,016
Yeah, he really does.

302
00:15:23,436 --> 00:15:25,012
Mr. Sponza.

303
00:15:25,012 --> 00:15:27,783
Mr. Gong, long time no chat.

304
00:15:27,783 --> 00:15:29,316
I saw your email.

305
00:15:29,316 --> 00:15:30,632
You're visiting Italy?

306
00:15:30,632 --> 00:15:32,712
Yes, for some coffee.

307
00:15:32,712 --> 00:15:34,088
Right.

308
00:15:34,088 --> 00:15:36,228
Italy is the place for coffee.

309
00:15:36,228 --> 00:15:38,828
I'll email you for a specific date.

310
00:15:38,828 --> 00:15:40,420
Don't mail. Just tell me.

311
00:15:40,420 --> 00:15:41,420
I'll be there.

312
00:15:41,420 --> 00:15:42,783
Then I'll see you soon.

313
00:15:42,783 --> 00:15:44,232
I'll keep in touch.

314
00:15:44,232 --> 00:15:46,449
Yes, bye.

315
00:15:50,904 --> 00:15:52,424
Korea?

316
00:15:52,424 --> 00:15:54,696
Yeah, Hongsung.

317
00:15:54,696 --> 00:15:56,324
Is he coming because of Mr. Jung?

318
00:15:56,324 --> 00:15:57,768
Of course, he is.

319
00:15:57,768 --> 00:16:00,296
Then he won't come empty-handed.

320
00:16:00,296 --> 00:16:02,456
He'll bring a massive offer.

321
00:16:02,456 --> 00:16:05,192
My friend, whatever Hongsung brings, you know you can't touch my order, right?

322
00:16:05,192 --> 00:16:07,052
After all this time, you still don't know me?

323
00:16:07,052 --> 00:16:08,816
I'm disappointed.

324
00:16:15,049 --> 00:16:19,083
[42 minutes Before the Laknes Launch]

325
00:16:37,476 --> 00:16:39,572
- Wait a second. - What time is it now?

326
00:16:39,572 --> 00:16:41,736
It's 9:48.

327
00:16:41,736 --> 00:16:43,583
Don't.

328
00:16:43,583 --> 00:16:45,349
We need to take two at a time.

329
00:16:45,349 --> 00:16:47,816
Oh, okay.

330
00:16:47,816 --> 00:16:49,349
- That's it. - Gi Tae.

331
00:16:49,349 --> 00:16:51,116
- Up we go. - Ms. Jang.

332
00:16:51,116 --> 00:16:52,824
We're roughly on schedule.

333
00:16:52,824 --> 00:16:54,792
We're not sure yet. It's still a close call.

334
00:16:56,660 --> 00:16:58,716
Oh, Ji Hye, take this.

335
00:16:58,716 --> 00:16:59,716
- Two? - Yeah.

336
00:16:59,716 --> 00:17:01,416
You got this, you got this.

337
00:17:02,980 --> 00:17:05,083
I told you to wait a second.

338
00:17:08,732 --> 00:17:10,432
What? Why?

339
00:17:12,172 --> 00:17:14,216
Ji Hye, hurry, hurry.

340
00:17:15,949 --> 00:17:17,683
Hurry, hurry!

341
00:17:19,188 --> 00:17:20,888
Ugh...

342
00:17:27,716 --> 00:17:30,224
Why are you so late? I thought you weren't coming.

343
00:17:30,224 --> 00:17:32,116
We come in now because we're finally done.

344
00:17:32,116 --> 00:17:33,249
We pulled an all-nighter.

345
00:17:33,249 --> 00:17:35,800
So who told you to take delivery of the merchandise this late?

346
00:17:35,800 --> 00:17:37,092
Whatever, just give us some praise.

347
00:17:37,092 --> 00:17:39,388
What is there to praise? Drink this.

348
00:17:39,388 --> 00:17:41,849
I knew it's for us.

349
00:17:43,684 --> 00:17:45,464
Wow, you redid the display?

350
00:17:45,464 --> 00:17:47,016
You think we were just slacking off?

351
00:17:48,064 --> 00:17:50,124
- Come have some. - I haven't even had any.

352
00:17:50,124 --> 00:17:53,583
Mr. Gong, have some iced coffee.

353
00:17:57,960 --> 00:18:00,616
We're opening now. Get ready.

354
00:18:30,928 --> 00:18:32,816
Are they coming to our store?

355
00:18:32,816 --> 00:18:34,516
Is that our store?

356
00:18:46,549 --> 00:18:49,249
- It's over there, right? - Welcome to Laknes.

357
00:18:52,516 --> 00:18:53,783
Welcome.

358
00:18:53,783 --> 00:18:55,416
There's no need to run.

359
00:18:55,416 --> 00:18:57,849
Please line up around here.

360
00:19:04,049 --> 00:19:06,249
Please wait a moment.

361
00:19:15,116 --> 00:19:17,316
Please wait a moment.

362
00:19:48,749 --> 00:19:51,688
[Sponza]

363
00:19:51,688 --> 00:19:53,716
Oh, one moment.

364
00:20:00,736 --> 00:20:01,856
Mr. Sponza?

365
00:20:01,856 --> 00:20:03,120
Mr. Jung.

366
00:20:03,120 --> 00:20:04,460
Sorry for the late call.

367
00:20:04,460 --> 00:20:05,664
It's okay.

368
00:20:05,664 --> 00:20:07,049
Where is the delivery?

369
00:20:07,049 --> 00:20:09,744
The guy from the warehouse mixed up the schedule.

370
00:20:09,744 --> 00:20:11,156
This never happened before.

371
00:20:11,156 --> 00:20:12,383
Okay.

372
00:20:12,383 --> 00:20:14,340
I'll let you handle the issue.

373
00:20:14,340 --> 00:20:16,949
So when is the departure?

374
00:20:16,949 --> 00:20:18,388
Within a week.

375
00:20:18,388 --> 00:20:21,020
I'll let you know when the schedule is ready.

376
00:20:21,020 --> 00:20:22,296
Okay.

377
00:20:22,296 --> 00:20:25,216
Oh, and Hongsung called.

378
00:20:26,080 --> 00:20:28,088
What did they say?

379
00:20:28,088 --> 00:20:30,116
They want to come in person.

380
00:20:31,940 --> 00:20:33,908
You don't have to worry, Mr. Jung.

381
00:20:33,908 --> 00:20:35,608
I'll handle this.

382
00:20:36,940 --> 00:20:38,612
Okay, thank you.

383
00:20:38,612 --> 00:20:40,312
Bye.

384
00:20:52,049 --> 00:20:54,528
Mr. Gong, have some coffee.

385
00:20:54,528 --> 00:20:56,416
- Thanks. - Sure.

386
00:20:58,496 --> 00:20:59,849
Did you get some rest?

387
00:20:59,849 --> 00:21:02,949
Oh, yes. I rested well.

388
00:21:02,949 --> 00:21:05,449
Good. Because you're going on a business trip.

389
00:21:06,140 --> 00:21:07,416
Pardon?

390
00:21:07,416 --> 00:21:10,216
You're coming to Italy with me this time.

391
00:21:12,444 --> 00:21:14,376
- I'm going? - Yes.

392
00:21:14,376 --> 00:21:16,492
It's about time you went on one.

393
00:21:16,492 --> 00:21:19,449
Oh, okay. Got it, sir.

394
00:21:19,449 --> 00:21:21,772
Will this be your first time in Italy?

395
00:21:21,772 --> 00:21:23,804
Yes, I've never been there.

396
00:21:23,804 --> 00:21:26,449
Oh, that's a shame.

397
00:21:26,449 --> 00:21:30,216
You're going to Italy, but you won't get to see any of it.

398
00:21:30,216 --> 00:21:31,240
Pardon?

399
00:21:31,240 --> 00:21:32,596
You'll see when you get there.

400
00:21:32,596 --> 00:21:34,716
That's how business trips are.

401
00:21:41,016 --> 00:21:42,716
I see.

402
00:22:32,816 --> 00:22:35,816
[Mantua, Italy]

403
00:22:50,632 --> 00:22:52,332
This way.

404
00:23:08,416 --> 00:23:10,583
Incredible.

405
00:23:13,288 --> 00:23:14,988
Whoa!

406
00:23:19,056 --> 00:23:21,283
Wow.

407
00:23:22,516 --> 00:23:25,016
Mr. Gong, these are all limited editions?

408
00:23:34,876 --> 00:23:36,276
Excuse me.

409
00:23:36,276 --> 00:23:37,976
Follow me please.

410
00:23:39,124 --> 00:23:40,849
Gi Tae?

411
00:23:50,360 --> 00:23:52,283
Well, Mr. Gong.

412
00:23:53,556 --> 00:23:55,732
Can I ask you something?

413
00:23:55,732 --> 00:23:57,996
Of course.

414
00:23:57,996 --> 00:24:02,016
Why did you bring me on this trip?

415
00:24:03,964 --> 00:24:06,283
You asked the exact same thing I did.

416
00:24:07,428 --> 00:24:09,124
Pardon?

417
00:24:09,124 --> 00:24:11,434
So you won't be surprised like that again

418
00:24:11,434 --> 00:24:13,749
when you come to the Italian warehouses.

419
00:24:16,924 --> 00:24:17,992
Mr. Gong!

420
00:24:17,992 --> 00:24:19,816
Mr. Sponza.

421
00:24:22,552 --> 00:24:25,032
This is Gi Tae Park from my company.

422
00:24:25,032 --> 00:24:26,628
You must be the next Mr. Gong.

423
00:24:26,628 --> 00:24:27,983
Nice to meet you, Mr. Park.

424
00:24:27,983 --> 00:24:31,268
Oh! Nice to meet you, Mr. Sponza.

425
00:24:31,268 --> 00:24:33,680
Good to meet you too.

426
00:24:33,680 --> 00:24:35,380
Have a seat.

427
00:24:42,796 --> 00:24:44,456
I miss this.

428
00:24:44,456 --> 00:24:46,960
Korean coffee is good too, no?

429
00:24:46,960 --> 00:24:48,436
It's not the same at all.

430
00:24:48,436 --> 00:24:51,672
Come often. Just say they are all business trips.

431
00:24:51,672 --> 00:24:53,348
Wish I can.

432
00:24:53,348 --> 00:24:56,052
You can have as much coffee as you want.

433
00:24:56,052 --> 00:24:57,908
Let's wrap up here and go eat.

434
00:24:57,908 --> 00:25:00,616
I've booked a perfect restaurant.

435
00:25:00,616 --> 00:25:03,483
By the way, what brings you here?

436
00:25:05,560 --> 00:25:09,764
You know Mr. Jung, who used to work with us, is dealing with Mantua.

437
00:25:09,764 --> 00:25:12,049
We'd appreciate it if you could cancel that

438
00:25:12,049 --> 00:25:15,583
and block him from all Mantua warehouses.

439
00:25:17,648 --> 00:25:20,036
Maybe there's something I'm missing.

440
00:25:20,036 --> 00:25:23,716
It feels like a lot for a small breakaway from Hongsung.

441
00:25:24,780 --> 00:25:28,932
He made a secret attempt to poach our employees.

442
00:25:28,932 --> 00:25:31,052
I see.

443
00:25:31,052 --> 00:25:33,256
Mr. Jung made a bad move.

444
00:25:33,256 --> 00:25:36,180
People can get shot here in Italy.

445
00:25:36,180 --> 00:25:39,549
So, can you do that?

446
00:25:42,056 --> 00:25:44,484
We can't just cancel it now.

447
00:25:44,484 --> 00:25:47,360
The invoice is done, and the shipment is ready to go.

448
00:25:47,360 --> 00:25:51,183
Mr. Jung probably use our name to lock in retail accounts.

449
00:25:51,183 --> 00:25:54,364
And this could ruin our reputation.

450
00:25:54,364 --> 00:25:57,420
I totally understand Hongsung's action, but honestly,

451
00:25:57,420 --> 00:26:00,316
it's too late to break the deal now.

452
00:26:02,316 --> 00:26:05,996
Sure, we can't just ask you to break the deal.

453
00:26:05,996 --> 00:26:08,624
We'll launch a select shop for luxury shoes

454
00:26:08,624 --> 00:26:11,683
and get Mantua to take care of the supply.

455
00:26:12,552 --> 00:26:14,956
This is why you're so confident.

456
00:26:14,956 --> 00:26:18,649
It must be a huge deal if you want us to risk our reputation.

457
00:26:27,624 --> 00:26:29,348
This is what we need.

458
00:26:29,348 --> 00:26:31,183
Please take a look.

459
00:26:32,849 --> 00:26:35,252
Three million euros for the first order,

460
00:26:35,252 --> 00:26:37,680
and 10 million for yearly orders.

461
00:26:37,680 --> 00:26:39,380
What do you think?

462
00:26:41,484 --> 00:26:45,116
You put me in a very difficult spot, Mr. Gong.

463
00:26:45,996 --> 00:26:47,696
One moment.

464
00:26:58,968 --> 00:27:01,783
Oh, I should've recorded that.

465
00:27:02,744 --> 00:27:04,364
The deal isn't over yet.

466
00:27:04,364 --> 00:27:05,704
Pardon?

467
00:27:05,704 --> 00:27:08,016
It wouldn't be Sponza if it ended like this.

468
00:27:08,792 --> 00:27:10,492
Have a drink.

469
00:27:17,348 --> 00:27:21,960
I canceled all of Mr. Jung's orders and delayed the shipment too.

470
00:27:21,960 --> 00:27:24,383
The other warehouses will do the same.

471
00:27:25,332 --> 00:27:26,884
Good. Thank you.

472
00:27:26,884 --> 00:27:30,516
But, there is one problem.

473
00:27:37,220 --> 00:27:40,552
What do you mean? The shipments are on hold?

474
00:27:40,552 --> 00:27:42,149
No, no, that can't be.

475
00:27:42,149 --> 00:27:44,192
Please check again.

476
00:27:44,192 --> 00:27:45,380
Okay?

477
00:27:45,380 --> 00:27:48,383
Hello? Hello!

478
00:27:49,068 --> 00:27:50,649
Darn it, seriously.

479
00:28:01,983 --> 00:28:03,364
The subscriber you are calling is not available.

480
00:28:03,364 --> 00:28:06,316
Darn it, Sponza, come on.

481
00:28:27,683 --> 00:28:29,528
Emilio.

482
00:28:29,528 --> 00:28:30,616
Sponza, I told you, huh?

483
00:28:30,616 --> 00:28:32,464
Don't touch my order.

484
00:28:32,464 --> 00:28:34,168
I heard you, so that's why I'm asking nicely.

485
00:28:34,168 --> 00:28:35,878
I don't care how much you deal with Hongsung,

486
00:28:35,878 --> 00:28:38,116
but I'm never canceling this shipment.

487
00:28:38,912 --> 00:28:41,449
May I ask why you're refusing?

488
00:28:43,392 --> 00:28:44,708
He speaks Italian?

489
00:28:44,708 --> 00:28:46,128
I didn't know either.

490
00:28:46,128 --> 00:28:47,692
I'm still learning.

491
00:28:47,692 --> 00:28:52,449
If I knew why you're refusing, I might be able to help.

492
00:28:53,908 --> 00:28:57,352
Okay. My daughter designed this shipment.

493
00:28:57,352 --> 00:29:00,616
I divorced my ex-wife and wasn't much of a father to her.

494
00:29:00,616 --> 00:29:03,868
This is the first order for my daughter's products.

495
00:29:03,868 --> 00:29:06,808
And you want me to cancel it myself? Absolutely not.

496
00:29:06,808 --> 00:29:08,820
May I ask what kind of product it is?

497
00:29:08,820 --> 00:29:09,980
Sunglasses.

498
00:29:09,980 --> 00:29:14,020
How much is Mr. Jung's total order, including the sunglasses?

499
00:29:14,020 --> 00:29:16,349
About 900,000 euros.

500
00:29:26,888 --> 00:29:28,616
What?

501
00:29:29,776 --> 00:29:31,228
Wait, how did that happen?

502
00:29:31,228 --> 00:29:32,708
That's how it turned out.

503
00:29:32,708 --> 00:29:35,128
I'll gather all the relevant documents and send them to you.

504
00:29:35,128 --> 00:29:38,984
Please have everything ready, so I can report as soon as I get back to Korea.

505
00:29:38,984 --> 00:29:43,604
Sure, I'll prepare the documents, but what happened?

506
00:29:43,604 --> 00:29:46,604
I had no choice if I wanted to close the deal.

507
00:29:46,604 --> 00:29:49,749
But did you really have to spend another 900,000 euros?

508
00:29:49,749 --> 00:29:51,340
Ugh, this is driving me crazy.

509
00:29:51,340 --> 00:29:53,308
I'll explain everything when I get back.

510
00:29:53,308 --> 00:29:55,216
Of course, you have to explain,

511
00:29:55,216 --> 00:29:56,688
- but right now... - Please handle it.

512
00:29:56,688 --> 00:29:59,349
Hello? Mr. Gong!

513
00:30:03,383 --> 00:30:05,016
What's gotten into him lately?

514
00:30:05,016 --> 00:30:06,149
Is he all excited again?

515
00:30:06,149 --> 00:30:07,849
Yeah.

516
00:30:09,516 --> 00:30:12,749
Jeez, Mr. Gong, what are you going to do?

517
00:30:13,783 --> 00:30:17,249
I've been doing things the way the company wanted long enough.

518
00:30:17,249 --> 00:30:19,332
Now I want to do things my way, at least this much.

519
00:30:19,332 --> 00:30:22,928
- What? - Worst case, I get fired. That's all.

520
00:30:22,928 --> 00:30:24,260
What?

521
00:30:24,260 --> 00:30:27,383
Wait, Mr. Gong! Mr. Gong!

522
00:30:45,483 --> 00:30:48,949
[Missed Call, Team Leader Jung Sun Hyuk, Team 4]

523
00:30:55,049 --> 00:30:58,116
Mr. Gong, you can take the taxi right in front.

524
00:30:58,116 --> 00:31:00,216
- Okay. - Alright, I'll be heading home.

525
00:31:00,216 --> 00:31:02,616
Good work. Get some rest.

526
00:31:02,616 --> 00:31:05,349
Could you open the trunk, please?

527
00:31:13,249 --> 00:31:15,116
Oh, wait, Mr. Gong,

528
00:31:16,424 --> 00:31:19,249
I learned a lot on this trip.

529
00:31:20,160 --> 00:31:21,860
Thank you.

530
00:31:25,344 --> 00:31:27,616
Wow, you really are just like me.

531
00:31:27,616 --> 00:31:29,316
Pardon?

532
00:31:31,604 --> 00:31:33,556
Nothing. See you tomorrow.

533
00:31:33,556 --> 00:31:36,049
Oh, yes, sir. Get home safely.

534
00:33:00,844 --> 00:33:02,544
You're back?

535
00:33:03,868 --> 00:33:06,648
You can't let yourself get this down.

536
00:33:06,648 --> 00:33:09,916
You're the CEO, for goodness' sake.

537
00:33:12,684 --> 00:33:14,649
Do I look discouraged to you?

538
00:33:34,028 --> 00:33:35,983
Hongsung is ruthless.

539
00:33:36,632 --> 00:33:38,683
Didn't you see this coming?

540
00:33:39,284 --> 00:33:42,049
I didn't think they'd go this far.

541
00:33:43,052 --> 00:33:45,283
Do you resent me?

542
00:33:46,848 --> 00:33:48,916
I resent myself.

543
00:33:49,848 --> 00:33:52,549
I was the one who first took you to Mantua.

544
00:33:53,820 --> 00:33:56,916
Wow... I took this kid who couldn't

545
00:33:56,916 --> 00:34:02,036
take his eyes off the warehouse and turned him into a real businessman,

546
00:34:02,036 --> 00:34:04,149
and this is how it comes back to me.

547
00:34:05,996 --> 00:34:07,488
You said it back then.

548
00:34:07,488 --> 00:34:11,049
"Don't be surprised when you come to the warehouse next time."

549
00:34:12,352 --> 00:34:14,052
Did I say that?

550
00:34:19,136 --> 00:34:21,049
Did I cross the line?

551
00:34:22,388 --> 00:34:26,012
No, even if I did,

552
00:34:26,012 --> 00:34:28,549
is this really a fair punishment?

553
00:34:38,852 --> 00:34:40,783
The shoe boutique,

554
00:34:42,816 --> 00:34:45,249
was it your idea or the company's?

555
00:34:46,948 --> 00:34:48,449
I led it.

556
00:34:48,449 --> 00:34:50,449
And the company agreed.

557
00:34:51,112 --> 00:34:52,812
I see.

558
00:34:59,372 --> 00:35:01,072
Mr. Jung,

559
00:35:02,076 --> 00:35:05,016
would you take the merchandise from me?

560
00:35:05,640 --> 00:35:06,672
What?

561
00:35:06,672 --> 00:35:11,483
It'll cost a little more than getting it directly from Mantua.

562
00:35:12,160 --> 00:35:13,449
What do you mean?

563
00:35:13,449 --> 00:35:14,749
Exactly what you heard.

564
00:35:14,749 --> 00:35:17,124
You won't be able to do business with Mantua anymore.

565
00:35:17,124 --> 00:35:20,583
If you want Mantua's merchandise, get it through Hongsung.

566
00:35:22,376 --> 00:35:24,304
The merchandise has already been shipped.

567
00:35:24,304 --> 00:35:29,200
Come to Hongsung this week and sign the contract in person.

568
00:35:29,200 --> 00:35:31,483
I'll convince the company.

569
00:35:32,964 --> 00:35:34,849
Are you saving me?

570
00:35:37,292 --> 00:35:39,083
I'll get going.

571
00:36:04,856 --> 00:36:06,649
You're here.

572
00:36:18,484 --> 00:36:20,492
Explain yourself.

573
00:36:20,492 --> 00:36:24,616
There was one warehouse owner who refused to cancel the deal.

574
00:36:25,388 --> 00:36:26,436
Come on.

575
00:36:26,436 --> 00:36:30,416
You're in front of the department head. Cut the crap and speak plainly.

576
00:36:31,376 --> 00:36:34,083
I didn't want to destroy Mr. Jung.

577
00:36:36,616 --> 00:36:39,520
Then what about Ms. Park and me?

578
00:36:39,520 --> 00:36:42,936
Then did the other team leaders want to destroy him?

579
00:36:42,936 --> 00:36:45,449
No. It seems like no one wants that.

580
00:36:47,432 --> 00:36:49,088
All of Mr. Jung's orders

581
00:36:49,088 --> 00:36:51,744
will be counted as our company's sales.

582
00:36:51,744 --> 00:36:54,716
At the same time, I believe we've made our stance clear internally

583
00:36:54,716 --> 00:36:57,583
about employees leaving improperly.

584
00:36:58,720 --> 00:37:00,908
So you're saying it's good for everyone?

585
00:37:00,908 --> 00:37:03,149
Yes. I believe so.

586
00:37:05,592 --> 00:37:09,184
So you exceeded the approved budget by 30%.

587
00:37:09,184 --> 00:37:12,372
Even if it comes back as company revenue,

588
00:37:12,372 --> 00:37:17,660
do you think a team leader should make that decision alone?

589
00:37:17,660 --> 00:37:21,908
What were you going to do if I refused to approve this?

590
00:37:21,908 --> 00:37:24,849
I negotiated on behalf of Hongsung,

591
00:37:26,724 --> 00:37:30,060
and I believe I got the best possible result.

592
00:37:30,060 --> 00:37:31,972
Yeah.

593
00:37:31,972 --> 00:37:34,816
It's my responsibility for sending you to Mantua.

594
00:37:37,616 --> 00:37:43,216
For the time being, Team 5 reports every order directly to me.

595
00:37:43,216 --> 00:37:46,588
Get my approval before spending a single won.

596
00:37:46,588 --> 00:37:48,416
Yes, ma'am.

597
00:37:49,916 --> 00:37:53,204
And there's one thing you're mistaken about.

598
00:37:53,204 --> 00:37:57,149
Do you think Mr. Jung is going to thank you?

599
00:38:09,656 --> 00:38:11,888
Is Team Leader Son late again today?

600
00:38:11,888 --> 00:38:14,349
This company is a complete mess.

601
00:38:22,884 --> 00:38:24,584
Sir!

602
00:38:33,049 --> 00:38:38,049
[Rest in Peace, CEO of Hongsung International]

603
00:38:44,549 --> 00:38:46,872
I heard he'd been bedridden for a long time.

604
00:38:46,872 --> 00:38:50,540
Still, he passed away peacefully.

605
00:38:50,540 --> 00:38:53,704
You should've told us.

606
00:38:53,704 --> 00:38:56,549
It's not exactly something I'd go around announcing.

607
00:38:58,872 --> 00:39:01,904
I should've checked in. I'm sorry.

608
00:39:01,904 --> 00:39:03,604
It's okay.

609
00:39:34,016 --> 00:39:35,532
[Condolence Box]

610
00:39:35,532 --> 00:39:36,916
You're here.

611
00:39:36,916 --> 00:39:39,216
The chief mourner is inside.

612
00:39:39,996 --> 00:39:41,749
You can go in.

613
00:39:43,636 --> 00:39:45,336
Hello.

614
00:39:59,600 --> 00:40:02,388
Isn't company life fascinating?

615
00:40:02,388 --> 00:40:05,316
Even after fighting tooth and nail,

616
00:40:05,316 --> 00:40:11,016
yet when it matters, everyone steps up like they never fought.

617
00:40:11,016 --> 00:40:14,883
I know. Maybe that's how they all manage to keep going.

618
00:40:17,488 --> 00:40:21,056
I heard you're supplying Mr. Jung's company.

619
00:40:21,056 --> 00:40:22,872
Yes, that's what happened.

620
00:40:22,872 --> 00:40:24,980
Good for you.

621
00:40:24,980 --> 00:40:27,452
Did I really do the right thing?

622
00:40:27,452 --> 00:40:29,336
He was like family once.

623
00:40:29,336 --> 00:40:32,448
It's not like we don't know his situation.

624
00:40:32,448 --> 00:40:35,783
What? Wait, is that Mr. Jung?

625
00:40:41,848 --> 00:40:42,848
You're here.

626
00:40:42,848 --> 00:40:45,040
Yeah. It's been a while.

627
00:40:45,040 --> 00:40:46,948
You're here.

628
00:40:46,948 --> 00:40:48,168
Let's go inside.

629
00:40:48,168 --> 00:40:51,500
No, I was going to call you when I got here.

630
00:40:51,500 --> 00:40:53,200
Just pay my respects for me.

631
00:40:54,384 --> 00:40:56,524
You came all this way, so please go in.

632
00:40:56,524 --> 00:40:58,260
It's better if I just leave.

633
00:40:58,260 --> 00:40:59,960
Here.

634
00:41:01,016 --> 00:41:04,383
[Condolence]

635
00:41:11,788 --> 00:41:14,883
I'm off. Take good care of him.

636
00:41:14,883 --> 00:41:19,416
[Baeksan University Funeral Hall]

637
00:41:46,249 --> 00:41:47,383
You are from Hongsung, right?

638
00:41:47,383 --> 00:41:49,164
Yes, we are with Hongsung.

639
00:41:49,164 --> 00:41:51,056
Where's the other truck?

640
00:41:51,056 --> 00:41:52,960
We only have one. Why do you ask?

641
00:41:52,960 --> 00:41:56,349
What are you talking about? These are all for Hongsung.

642
00:42:00,288 --> 00:42:02,004
Wait, all of these are for Hongsung?

643
00:42:02,004 --> 00:42:03,336
Yeah.

644
00:42:03,336 --> 00:42:04,692
Huh? That can't be right.

645
00:42:04,692 --> 00:42:06,483
What do you mean, it can't be?

646
00:42:06,483 --> 00:42:08,356
Just go check, quickly.

647
00:42:08,356 --> 00:42:09,356
Can I get a bottle of liquor, please?

648
00:42:09,356 --> 00:42:11,876
- A drink? Just a moment. - Yes.

649
00:42:11,876 --> 00:42:14,572
Ji Hye... Ji Hye!

650
00:42:14,572 --> 00:42:17,383
I'll bring it right over. Just a moment.

651
00:42:18,216 --> 00:42:19,749
- Thank you. - Sure.

652
00:42:19,749 --> 00:42:23,049
[Lee Min Ho, Hongsung Logistics Team]

653
00:42:42,249 --> 00:42:43,483
[Six Years Ago]

654
00:42:43,483 --> 00:42:45,616
Huh? Team Leader, good morning.

655
00:42:45,616 --> 00:42:47,116
Yeah.

656
00:42:47,116 --> 00:42:48,449
Did you drink last night?

657
00:42:48,449 --> 00:42:50,036
Yeah, I did.

658
00:42:50,036 --> 00:42:52,083
How much did you drink?

659
00:42:52,083 --> 00:42:54,196
Way too freaking much.

660
00:42:54,196 --> 00:42:57,556
Then I'll make you some delicious honey water.

661
00:42:57,556 --> 00:42:59,749
Thanks a ton!

662
00:43:05,040 --> 00:43:07,132
Darn it.

663
00:43:07,132 --> 00:43:09,149
- Hey. - Yes?

664
00:43:10,040 --> 00:43:11,876
Do you buy lottery tickets?

665
00:43:11,876 --> 00:43:13,683
Well, sometimes.

666
00:43:13,683 --> 00:43:16,892
Don't do it sometimes. Do it every week.

667
00:43:16,892 --> 00:43:21,849
What other hope do office workers like us have?

668
00:43:25,616 --> 00:43:26,616
Did you win?

669
00:43:26,616 --> 00:43:29,383
[Unfortunately, you did not win]

670
00:43:30,944 --> 00:43:33,883
Like that'd happen. Darn it.

671
00:43:33,883 --> 00:43:35,684
Jeez.

672
00:43:35,684 --> 00:43:37,683
You got this, Team Leader.

673
00:43:38,516 --> 00:43:41,083
[Staff Member Gong Eun Tae]

674
00:43:42,272 --> 00:43:44,104
We're having jjamppong for lunch.

675
00:43:44,104 --> 00:43:45,804
Thank you.

676
00:43:46,652 --> 00:43:48,180
Did Team Leader drink?

677
00:43:48,180 --> 00:43:50,316
Yeah, he said a whole freaking lot.

678
00:43:51,932 --> 00:43:53,820
Did you check the lottery ticket?

679
00:43:53,820 --> 00:43:55,964
If it wins, we split it, remember?

680
00:43:55,964 --> 00:43:58,216
A dud for sure. Did you check?

681
00:43:58,216 --> 00:44:00,083
I'm about to check right now.

682
00:44:00,783 --> 00:44:03,716
[Congratulations! You won 50,000 won]

683
00:44:05,149 --> 00:44:06,516
It's a dud, right?

684
00:44:11,756 --> 00:44:13,749
Like that'd happen. Darn it.

685
00:44:15,696 --> 00:44:18,416
Jeez, winning the lotto is tough.

686
00:44:23,440 --> 00:44:25,440
MkvDrama.net
